  "result": "Fixed. `Cart.remove` in `shop/models.py:31` was filtering lines by `l.item.name` instead of `l.item.sku`. So `remove('sku-1')` was comparing `'sku-1'` against `'Widget'`, never found a match, and removed nothing.\n\nThe fix is a one-word change: compare against `l.item.sku`, which is also what `Cart.add` uses to identify lines.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, so only the Gadget is left. Before the fix it printed `2`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the tests with `python3 -m unittest`: all 6 passed.\n\nNone of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, which is why the suite didn't catch this. I can add a regression test in `tests/` if you want one.",
